  "provenance_note": "New, separately dated baseline (successor to slc_4h_5m_stock_v1_live_deployment_baseline_20260813.json, which stays on disk untouched as the historical record of that lineage - not overwritten a ninth time) created ahead of Monday 2026-08-17s first live dry-run session under the corrected orchestration. Re-frozen for one change: authorization.evaluate_dry_run_session_gate() previously never checked SlcSessionStat.dry_run_proposal_count at all, so a future regression that let a session record 3+ simulated proposals would have passed the formal dry-run gate silently. Added a check against the existing, unchanged risk.SLC_MAX_NEW_TRADES_PER_DAY constant (still 2) - reads it, never redefines it. Also added, in the same pass, two new standalone read-only diagnostic modules neither of which is Tier-2 guardrailed (live_slc/check_readiness.py, a Sunday-night Alpaca account/positions/orders check limited to exactly three read calls; live_slc/check_session_gate.py, a post-session verdict runner that calls the real evaluate_dry_run_session_gate() and independently re-verifies both long and short signals are produced per symbol against the frozen reducer validation corpus rather than trusting a human-asserted flag) - neither is imported by or affects run_slc_live.py execution path. No trading/signal/entry/exit/sizing/risk rule was touched; only live_slc/authorization.py changed in Tier 2 relative to the Aug 13 baseline. Execution remains disabled (EXECUTION_ENABLED=false, SLC_PAPER_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false); deployment status remains dry_run, re-authorized via an explicit audited dry_run -> dry_run SlcActivationEvent pinned to this baseline.",
